6. Elliptic Curve Cryptography (ECC)
ECC uses mathematical operations on elliptic curves. It provides strong security with comparatively short keys.
ECC is used in digital signatures and key agreement, particularly in modern communication systems.
Conclusion: Public-key cryptography evolved from early key-distribution research into a fundamental technology used in secure internet communication.
